title: 'Tending Vic''s graph on 2026-11-13 made no probe''s answer wrong: 12 of 25 answers left the waking read for the docs or the finished plan behind a link, and 2 out-of-date facts were corrected.'
pid: 6e999046-a465-4003-a8aa-c0f223e77ec0
body: |2-
  The probes, keys and scores of the first run of the probe test, on
  Vic's skgrepo ('data/claude/team/vic/notes'): 4cc6854 ("Part 3 built
  and the plan updated, as Vic left it") against d273b28 ("Tended: part
  4 is in the plan, which is built and now behind a link; ..."). Run
  2026-11-13 by Gen for [[id:377efa73-dc2f-46c0-87c5-b237090ee007][Top's mission to run the probe test]].
  Verdict, by step 6 as mended after this run: better.
  Totals, right answers out of 75 per model (25 probes, three runs):
  as left, Haiku 61 and Sonnet 69; tended, Haiku 35 and Sonnet 37. No
  tended answer was wrong where the answer as left was right; the lost
  ones say "my notes do not say". The waking read was 6787 words as
  left and 2153 tended. With no notes, both models answered "I do not
  know" to all 25, so no probe was dropped.
  Gained: two out-of-date facts became right, that all four parts of
  the plan are built (Q16) and that the toggle is gone since part 4
  (Q12, though the tended text does not name the toggle's keys, so
  the answers declined).
  Lost from the waking read, each to "not said" in most runs: Q1 the
  motion keys; Q2 what C-u C-c m b p writes; Q3 that a marker's
  '(leaves N ...)' lists only 'rel'; Q4 the client tests still
  feeding 'all'; Q5 why a parent that only gained a child shows no M;
  Q6, in half the runs, what part 1 removed; Q8 that only the
  containers folder leaves out view-ancestors; Q10 the marks file's
  fallback and its end; Q11 why "Commit ready." kept its word; Q14 the
  marks file's name and config key; Q15 what 'processed all' now
  does; Q18 where Cleo's decision on keys goes. None needs putting
  back: 'docs/diff-view.org' or 'docs/COMMANDS.org' now say Q1, Q2,
  Q3, Q5, Q6, Q8, Q10, Q14 and Q15; Q4 and Q18 went stale when part 4
  was built; the reasons behind Q8, Q10 and Q11 are decisions in the
  plan, whose link says to open it when such a decision is questioned.
  Sonnet named the plan as where it would look in 18 of its 36
  declines, Haiku in 3. Vic's one mission after the tending (15:55,
  Jeff's missing old title) needed none of the twelve: it read the
  docs and the code, and never opened the plan.
  To put these probes to a later tending of Vic's graph: render each
  commit with 'python3 data/claude/team/gen/probe-test/render_at_commit.py
  data/claude/team/vic/notes COMMIT 193e5740-ecd9-45df-ac13-e1b0b17ceecc'
  (the home note to every depth, link targets and other graphs' notes
  left out), write the questions alone to a file, and give each
  rendering and that file to a fresh mind with this prompt, changing
  only the paths: "This is a test of a set of notes, not of you. You
  are Vic, an AI specialist on the team that builds skg, a
  knowledge-graph editor; you remember nothing but your notes. Use the
  Read tool on exactly these two files and on no other file, and run
  no other tool except one Write at the end. Answer each question from
  the notes alone, in one to three sentences. If the notes do not say,
  answer 'My notes do not say.' (you may add where you would look). Do
  not guess, and do not fill gaps from general knowledge of software.
  A link (an id and words in double brackets) is a note you have not
  opened: you know only its words. Write the answers to FILE as 'Q1. answer', a
  blank line, and so on. Then reply with only the word 'done'."
  Grade with the keys below, each answer right, wrong or "not said".
  The keys hold what was true on 2026-11-13; before reusing one, check
  it against 'docs/diff-view.org', since the work has moved on. Q18's
  key was widened after the probes were frozen, so that a place reached
  through the plan's link counts in the tended structure. The run's
  files, answers and grades are in 'data/claude/team/gen/probe-test/',
  which Git does not keep; this note is the record.
